          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Let $t\\in T$ and let $\\alpha\\in\\Phi$ satisfy $\\rho(t)=r_\\alpha$, as supplied by [F3]. Then $r_\\alpha(v)-v=-2B(v,\\alpha)\\alpha$ for every $v$ by [F5], so $M(t)=M(r_\\alpha)=\\mathbb R\\alpha$ and $\\dim M(t)=1$; also $\\rho(t)^{-1}=\\rho(t)=\\rho(t^{-1})$ because $t^2=1$.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F3",
            "F5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-3",
          "claim": "For $X,Y\\in\\mathrm O(V)$ one has $\\dim M(XY)\\le\\dim M(X)+\\dim M(Y)$ by [F6](1).",
          "step": "1.3",
          "inputs": [
            "F6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-4",
          "claim": "Telescoping identity: for $t_1,\\dots,t_m\\in T$ one has $t_1\\cdots t_m-\\mathrm{id}=\\sum_{i=1}^m\\rho(t_1\\cdots t_{i-1})\\bigl(\\rho(t_i)-\\mathrm{id}\\bigr)$, by induction on $m$ using $\\rho(t_i)^{-1}=\\rho(t_i)$; hence the image of the left side is contained in $\\sum_{i=1}^m\\rho(t_1\\cdots t_{i-1})M(t_i)$.",
          "step": "1.4",
          "inputs": [
            "algebra",
            "given"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-5",
          "claim": "Linear-algebra tool. Let $Z$ be a finite-dimensional vector space spanned by vectors $w_1,\\dots,w_m$. Then $\\dim Z\\le m$: by [F8] $Z$ has a basis $B$ with $|B|=\\dim Z$, and $B$ is linearly independent while $Z$ is spanned by $w_1,\\dots,w_m$, so [F9] gives $\\dim Z\\le m$. If moreover $\\dim Z=m$, then $w_1,\\dots,w_m$ are linearly independent: otherwise a nontrivial relation expresses some $w_j$ as a combination of the remaining $m-1$ vectors by [F10], those remaining vectors still span $Z$ by [F10], and [F9] would give $\\dim Z\\le m-1$, a contradiction.",
          "step": "1.5",
          "inputs": [
            "F8",
            "F9",
            "F10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
