        {
          "id": "step-2-3",
          "claim": "Let $t_1,\\dots,t_m\\in T$ and put $v_i:=\\rho(t_1\\cdots t_{i-1})\\alpha_i$, where $\\alpha_i\\in\\Phi$ satisfies $\\rho(t_i)=r_{\\alpha_i}$. By step 1.4 the space $M(t_1\\cdots t_m)$ is contained in $\\sum_i\\rho(t_1\\cdots t_{i-1})M(t_i)=\\sum_i\\mathbb Rv_i$ by step 1.2, so it is spanned by the $m$ vectors $v_1,\\dots,v_m$ and $\\dim M(t_1\\cdots t_m)\\le m$ by step 1.5.",
